A recommendation is a category-A-recommendation and is an evidence-type-2-recommendation.
If a patient has a subacute-pain and a nonopioid-therapy is appropriate for the patient then every clinician should maximize the nonopioid-therapy for the subacute-pain.
If a patient has a chronic-pain and a nonopioid-therapy is appropriate for the patient then every clinician should maximize the nonopioid-therapy for the chronic-pain.
If a patient has a subacute-pain then every nonopioid-therapy is preferred for the subacute-pain.
If a patient has a chronic-pain then every nonopioid-therapy is preferred for the chronic-pain.
If an opioid-benefit does not likely outweigh an opioid-risk and there is a clinician then it is recommended that the clinician does not consider an opioid-therapy.
Every clinician should discuss a realistic-benefit with a patient before an initiation.
Every clinician should discuss a known-risk with a patient before an initiation.
Every clinician should establish a pain-goal with a patient.
Every clinician should establish a function-goal with a patient.
If an opioid-benefit does not outweigh an opioid-risk then every clinician should consider a discontinuation.
